From f9a624dd62d3b327de17742b2ad935e1068c0156 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johnny Collado <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:04:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enable SSE4.1 for GCC/Clang on x86-64

The runtime and generated code use SSE4.1 intrinsics (_mm_extract_epi32/64,
_mm_blendv_ps, _mm_min_epi32), which MSVC accepts without a flag. GCC and Clang
refuse to inline them unless the target is enabled, so Linux builds failed in
ps2_memory.cpp and ps2_runtime.cpp. Add -msse4.1 for non-MSVC x86-64 builds,
next to the existing ARM flags.

Tested on Linux: GCC 13 and Clang, Release; ps2x_tests 445/445, the GS cache
tests and runELFtests pass on both. Android arm64 (NDK r27c) is unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index c7c7af5..44089d1 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -77,6 +77,11 @@ if(PS2X_IS_ARM_TARGET)
             add_compile_options(-march=armv8-a+fp+simd)
         endif()
     endif()
+elseif(NOT MSVC AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "x86_64|AMD64|amd64")
+    # The runtime and generated code use SSE4.1 intrinsics (_mm_extract_epi32/64, _mm_blendv_ps...).
+    # MSVC accepts them without a flag; GCC and Clang need the target enabled.
+    message(STATUS "x86-64 target with GCC/Clang - enabling SSE4.1")
+    add_compile_options(-msse4.1)
 endif()
 
 if(PS2X_BUILD_RECOMP)
